  "name": "Peggy Gou",
  "entity_type": "person",
  "description": "Peggy Gou has had a stellar 12 months, beginning with a sold-out headline show at London’s Drumsheds, followed by an Australia tour with pit stops in Melbourne and Sydney. She also continued her open-air sets trend — Palais Royal in Paris, on the Thames in London — leaning into her penchant for sun-soaked, high-fashion festival curations. Other highlights include shows at Ultra Japan, Solomon+1 at Pacha Ibiza, Kappa FuturFestival and her Midnight Lobster Club series, which Gou launched at [UNVRS]. She had some down time in the studio too, putting a Hi-NRG twist on Madonna’s ‘I Feel So Free’, and dropping Ayra Starr collab ‘Wo, man’.",
